## Context
Child of tracker 1309 (read its inventory and the wake probe in its
"Original wake context"). First child: it creates `scripts/runtime.py`, the
runtime twin of `scripts/forge.py`, and its first verb.

Probe already run (2026-10-28, padme): `codex queue --thread <id> --message`
starts a turn in a live, idle Codex session (positive control fired); into an
exited session it queues and nothing runs. Pi 1.4.0: an extension timer started
at `session_start` plus `pi.sendUserMessage()` should do it (docs only, untested).

## Shape
- `runtime.py [--runtime auto|claude|codex|pi] <verb> ...`, selection as in
  forge.py: a flag, `auto` detects from the runtime's own environment; an
  unknown runtime is reported, never guessed.
- `runtime.py can <verb>` exits 0/1. Unsupported verbs answer a typed NOOP
  (exit code + one line), never a silent pass.
- `wake arm --after <s> --cmd <cmd>`, `wake disarm`, `wake send --session <id>
  --message <text>`. Per backend: Claude Code, the background command whose exit
  re-invokes the session (the verb prints the command for the session to run in
  the background, since only the session's own tool can start it); Codex, an
  external timer that calls `codex queue`; Pi, a small extension under
  `adapters/pi/extensions/` that delivers queued wake files.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `scripts/runtime.py` with selection, `can`, typed NOOP, and `wake`
- [ ] tests/test_runtime.py with stubbed backends (like tests/test_forge.py), plus
      a positive and a negative control per backend
- [ ] Live positive control recorded for Pi and Codex (Codex: re-run the probe through
      runtime.py); Claude Code through the existing background path
- [ ] The wake sites listed in 1309 call `runtime.py`; "Codex and Pi have no timed
      wake" and "Claude Code only" lines removed; `scripts/check-agnostic.sh` passes
- [ ] `make check` passes
